From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 19:56:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] Add the cover picker to the studio
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A "Cover" button beside Save and Download on a finished video, opening a
grid of candidates.

Opening it extracts frames, which is free, so there is always something to
choose from the moment the dialog appears. "Generate cover options" is a
deliberate second step because it spends image credits, and it appears only
when the server says this video has a character to anchor covers to. The
aspect selector sits with that button rather than at the top of the dialog,
because it only affects generated covers — an extracted frame is whatever
shape the video is, and no crop turns a 9:16 frame into a usable 16:9 cover.

The current cover is seeded into the grid as the first tile, so changing
your mind needs no undo. New candidates append rather than replace: a tile
the user is reaching for stays the tile they hit.

